  "comments": "<p>KM#50.1 - Smaller lettering on Obverse.<br>KM#50.2 - Bigger lettering on Obverse.<br><br>There are 2 varieties in 1982, which are easy to distinguish by script.<br><br><i>Obverse</i><br>Die <strong>1</strong> - script thin.<br>Die <strong>2</strong> - script bold.<br><br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5d5af281d12dc.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5d5af281d12dc.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br><br>Schön attributes KM# 50.1 to the Royal Canadian Mint, KM# 50.2 die 1 (\"matted relief\") to the Karlsruhe mint, and die 2 (\"shiny relief with sharp contours\") to Paris.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Coin in plastic pocket from Monnaie de Paris. A small part of french mintage was selected as ESSAI but without marking on coin.</p><p>Image by Marcin Łysik</p><p><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/68c3c66f3fedf.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/68c3c66f3fedf.jpg\"></a></p>",
